{"name":"Cold Blooded","hex":"#bbeeee","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cold-blooded","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having an unregulated body temperature; ectothermic.","Lacking emotion or compunction."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cold-blooded"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ectotherm","blocks":[{"text":"An ectotherm, more commonly referred to as a \"cold-blooded animal\", is an animal in which internal physiological sources of heat, such as blood, are of relatively small or of quite negligible importance in controlling body temperature. Such organisms rely on environmental heat sources, which permit them to operate at very economical metabolic rates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Wiki_ostrich.jpg/330px-Wiki_ostrich.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ectotherm"},{"title":"Poikilotherm","blocks":[{"text":"A poikilotherm is an animal whose internal temperature varies considerably. Poikilotherms have to survive and adapt to environmental stress. One of the most important stressors is outer environment temperature change, which can lead to alterations in membrane lipid order and can cause protein unfolding and denaturation at elevated temperatures. Poikilotherm is the opposite of homeotherm – an animal which maintains thermal homeostasis. Usually the fluctuations are a consequence of variation in the ambient environmental temperature. Many terrestrial ectotherms are poikilothermic. However some ectotherms seek constant-temperature environments to the point that they are able to maintain a constant internal temperature, and are considered actual or practical homeotherms. It is this distinction that often makes the term poikilotherm more useful than the vernacular \"cold-blooded\", which is sometimes used to refer to ectotherms more generally."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Wiki_ostrich.jpg/330px-Wiki_ostrich.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poikilotherm"},{"title":"Cold Blooded (Rick James album)","blocks":[{"text":"Cold Blooded is the seventh studio album by American singer-songwriter and musician Rick James, released on the Gordy Records imprint of Motown Records. The title track was written with actress Linda Blair in mind, whom James was dating at the time."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/55/Rick_James_-_Cold_Blooded.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cold_Blooded_(Rick_James_album)"},{"title":"Cold Blooded (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Cold Blooded is a 2012 Canadian crime film written and directed by Jason Lapeyre. The film stars Ryan Robbins, Zoie Palmer, William MacDonald, Sergio Di Zio and Huse Madhavji. The film tells the story of a female police officer assigned to guard a diamond thief overnight in a hospital when his violent partners break into the hospital to get him."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3b/Cold_Blooded_-_Original_Theatrical_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cold_Blooded_(film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Basking_turtles.JPG/500px-Basking_turtles.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Basking_turtles.JPG/1280px-Basking_turtles.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Basking_turtles.JPG/500px-Basking_turtles.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pseudemys turtles (shown here basking for warmth) are ectothermic.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABasking_turtles.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/American_alligators_%28Alligator_mississippiensis%29%2C_Attwater_Prairie_Chicken_National_Wildlife_Refuge.jpg/500px-American_alligators_%28Alligator_mississippiensis%29%2C_Attwater_Prairie_Chicken_National_Wildlife_Refuge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/American_alligators_%28Alligator_mississippiensis%29%2C_Attwater_Prairie_Chicken_National_Wildlife_Refuge.jpg/960px-American_alligators_%28Alligator_mississippiensis%29%2C_Attwater_Prairie_Chicken_National_Wildlife_Refuge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/American_alligators_%28Alligator_mississippiensis%29%2C_Attwater_Prairie_Chicken_National_Wildlife_Refuge.jpg/500px-American_alligators_%28Alligator_mississippiensis%29%2C_Attwater_Prairie_Chicken_National_Wildlife_Refuge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmerican_alligators_(Alligator_mississippiensis)%2C_Attwater_Prairie_Chicken_National_Wildlife_Refuge.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Junonia_lemonias_DSF_by_Kadavoor.JPG/330px-Junonia_lemonias_DSF_by_Kadavoor.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Junonia_lemonias_DSF_by_Kadavoor.JPG/960px-Junonia_lemonias_DSF_by_Kadavoor.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Junonia_lemonias_DSF_by_Kadavoor.JPG/330px-Junonia_lemonias_DSF_by_Kadavoor.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJunonia_lemonias_DSF_by_Kadavoor.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/da/BLACK_SNAKE.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/da/BLACK_SNAKE.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABLACK_SNAKE.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/XBio_illustration_%E2%80%93_Poikilothermic.png/500px-XBio_illustration_%E2%80%93_Poikilothermic.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/XBio_illustration_%E2%80%93_Poikilothermic.png/1280px-XBio_illustration_%E2%80%93_Poikilothermic.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/XBio_illustration_%E2%80%93_Poikilothermic.png/500px-XBio_illustration_%E2%80%93_Poikilothermic.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Poikilothermic animals, also called cold blooded animals, whose internal temperatures fluctuate with their external environmental temperature.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AXBio_illustration_%E2%80%93_Poikilothermic.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Bgbo_frosch_ies.jpg/500px-Bgbo_frosch_ies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Bgbo_frosch_ies.jpg/500px-Bgbo_frosch_ies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The common frog is a poikilotherm and is able to function over a wide range of body core temperatures.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABgbo_frosch_ies.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thu